INTERVIEWED:  SCP-5133

INTERVIEWER:  Dr. Paul Gray

DATE OF LOG:  1/15/19 Approx. 12:15 Local Time
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[IRRELEVANT INFORMATION OMITTED — BEGIN LOG] 

Dr. Gray:  Excellent. To begin, how did you come to be?

SCP-5133:  *scratches* Human

Dr. Gray:  Right Were you once human?

SCP-5133:  I am

Dr. Gray:  So you are currently human?

SCP-5133's hand hesitates before writing.

SCP-5133:  Aren't I?

Dr. Gray:  No. You appear as the remains of a person.

SCP-5133 looks down at its hands and puts its hands to its face.

Dr. Gray:  Eh, hello?

SCP-5133 Lifts its hand and bangs the steel table once.

Dr. Gray:  Calm down. I've only got one more question.

SCP-5133 looks up at Dr. Gray

Dr. Gray:  Ok. Are you aware of your anomalous ability to disintegrate things?

SCP-5133 hesitates once more.

SCP-5133:  Too many questions

SCP-5133 places its hand on the protective glass between them and the glass starts to decay.

Dr. Gray calls off the interview as the glass starts cracking
[END LOG] 
